## Safety Rules

These rules apply regardless of which AI tool you use. See the full rationale in the [AI-Assisted Development Standards](https://github.com/planetary/.github/blob/main/standards/ai-assisted-development.md).

1. **No destructive git** — Never run checkout --, restore, reset, clean, stash drop, or force push without explicit permission.
2. **No untested claims** — Never claim code works without executing it. State assumptions clearly.
3. **No unauthorized push** — Never push, create PRs, or post comments without permission.
4. **No AI attribution** — No AI references in commits, PRs, or code comments.
5. **No file deletion** — Never delete files without safe backup and permission.

